From 3eb0fa2ee58ac001ba76f16c90b918efdb7e9fe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raold <868138+raold@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:53:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Let an external controller own a bot's tactics

AcquireExternalControl gives a caller (a training controller such as
mod-dojo) exclusive control of one bot under an epoch that is never
reused; ReleaseExternalControl takes only the current epoch and resets
the AI as a far teleport does, so stock behaviour resumes from a clean
state. Ownership lives in the PlayerbotAI and ends with it.

While owned, UpdateAI keeps its state checks and fall information and
returns before the cheat refill, the reaction engine, the preparing-cast
handling, the transport and group-master updates and UpdateAIInternal.
Chat commands and replies, the master's packets, DoSpecificAction,
DoNextAction, CastSpell, CastVehicleSpell and RequestSpellInterrupt are
refused and counted; the bot's own packets are dropped except root,
unroot, knockback and dismount. Teleport acks and session packets in
PlayerbotHolder are untouched. Inert until a caller acquires a bot.
